{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>With a wicked fist.</b> A hard thing with which one is struck, and in the words of the early ones of blessed memory, possessors of fists [Pesahim 53]; and like it: with a stone or with a fist (Exodus 21:18). And some say: a hard clod of earth, like מגרפותיהם (Joel 1:17)." "<b>You shall not fast as today.</b> Its meaning: like this day."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes מגרפותיהם in Hebrew script; Joel 1:17 is the correct verse reference for this word."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:06.114808197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}